1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,218
This guide assembles your R eight printed head.

2
00:00:03,438 --> 00:00:07,842
Match parts by shape and number; the colours are only for identification.

3
00:00:08,062 --> 00:00:12,379
Keep the video or PDF beside your bench, and pause after each step.

4
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,399
Lay out the fourteen prints.

5
00:00:17,619 --> 00:00:21,739
The open chassis is forty two; the long moving carriage is forty four.

6
00:00:21,959 --> 00:00:24,944
The thin rectangular spring is cassette fifty seven.

7
00:00:25,164 --> 00:00:28,911
Inspect its beams for cracks, separated layers or bowing.

8
00:00:29,131 --> 00:00:31,393
Coupon fifty three is a fit test.

9
00:00:31,613 --> 00:00:34,079
Bridge fifty five is a temporary tool.

10
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:40,091
Count the purchased hardware before starting.

11
00:00:40,311 --> 00:00:45,087
You need seven M two nuts and fourteen M three nuts, including three for the bridge.

12
00:00:45,307 --> 00:00:48,280
The four short adaptor screws must have button heads.

13
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:52,183
Also collect the real magnet, Hall sensor and capacitor.

14
00:00:52,403 --> 00:00:55,193
Use small hand tools, and tighten gently.

15
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,070
Turn the chassis over.

16
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:06,969
Fit four M three adaptor nuts, two M three sensor nuts, and two M two cassette nuts.

17
00:01:07,189 --> 00:01:11,249
A tiny adhesive tack can hold the deep cassette nuts; let it cure.

18
00:01:11,469 --> 00:01:15,422
Join adaptor forty one with four M three by eight button-head screws.

19
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:23,465
Work on carriage forty four outside the housing.

20
00:01:23,685 --> 00:01:28,210
Insert two M two nuts in the mounting posts and two in the magnet-retainer slots.

21
00:01:28,430 --> 00:01:32,800
Bond the six by three millimetre magnet with a thin adhesive layer and let it cure.

22
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:36,664
Then fit retainer forty six with two M two by ten screws.

23
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:47,680
Place the wide moving rail against the bottoms of the two carriage posts.

24
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:51,411
Drive two M two by eight screws upward from underneath the cassette.

25
00:01:51,631 --> 00:01:53,196
Their heads stay underneath.

26
00:01:53,416 --> 00:01:57,979
Complete this outside the housing, because the chassis floor blocks access later.

27
00:01:58,199 --> 00:02:00,096
Leave the narrow fixed rail free.

28
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:11,461
Seat the remaining M two nut in the receiver side slot, then fit the M two by twelve cartridge lock.

29
00:02:11,681 --> 00:02:13,418
Knob fifty one is optional.

30
00:02:13,638 --> 00:02:16,986
Leave this small lock loose so the cartridge path stays clear.

31
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:23,944
Lower the carriage and cassette together into the open chassis.

32
00:02:24,164 --> 00:02:27,051
Hold the solid parts, never the thin beams.

33
00:02:27,271 --> 00:02:32,816
Rest the narrow fixed rail on its two pads, and place the large shoulder between the lower stops.

34
00:02:33,036 --> 00:02:35,741
The rail holes should align without bending the spring.

35
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:41,279
Fit three M three nuts in bridge fifty five.

36
00:02:41,499 --> 00:02:47,133
Secure the bridge using the two front M three by thirty five cover screws, inserted from below.

37
00:02:47,353 --> 00:02:49,636
Add the M three by thirty service screw.

38
00:02:49,856 --> 00:02:53,568
It should enter the shoulder bore easily and hold the carriage near neutral.

39
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:03,652
Now insert the other two M two by eight screws downward from above through the narrow fixed rail.

40
00:03:03,872 --> 00:03:06,020
Tighten evenly with the cassette flat.

41
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:10,311
Remove the entire service screw and check gentle movement and free return.

42
00:03:10,531 --> 00:03:13,772
Stop if anything bows, rubs or stays displaced.

43
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:21,927
Solder and insulate the Hall sensor leads and decoupling capacitor before seating the package.

44
00:03:22,147 --> 00:03:24,443
Its flat face points toward the magnet.

45
00:03:24,663 --> 00:03:29,670
Secure mount forty seven with two M three by six screws, centred in the slots.

46
00:03:29,890 --> 00:03:34,053
Route and strain-relieve wires along fixed structure and out through the side port.

47
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,656
Remove the service screw and both bridge mounting screws.

48
00:03:42,876 --> 00:03:45,201
Set the bridge aside with its three nuts.

49
00:03:45,421 --> 00:03:50,032
Fit five M three nuts into cover forty three, including the service-screw nut.

50
00:03:50,252 --> 00:03:56,113
Check the wires, lower the cover, and fasten all four M three by thirty five screws from underneath.

51
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:05,347
For the first bench test, use rigid cartridge forty nine.

52
00:04:05,567 --> 00:04:08,437
With the tip unloaded, install the service screw.

53
00:04:08,657 --> 00:04:11,924
Back the small cartridge lock out at least three millimetres.

54
00:04:12,144 --> 00:04:18,758
Align the lugs, insert the cartridge, turn thirty degrees, seat the flange and gently tighten the small lock.

55
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:25,225
Remove the entire long service screw, not just its knob.

56
00:04:25,445 --> 00:04:27,725
Leave the small cartridge lock tightened.

57
00:04:27,945 --> 00:04:32,169
Check gentle axial movement and free return without forcing the stops.

58
00:04:32,389 --> 00:04:36,939
Then wire the external bench electronics and calibrate against a checked balance.

59
00:04:37,159 --> 00:04:40,689
The printed spring has no established force rating until tested.
